network-manager-vless (0.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Turn off another client's local system proxy while VLESS is connected
    (nm-vless-proxy-guard user service) and restore it afterwards.
  * Route 0.0.0.0/1 and 128.0.0.0/1 (::/1, 8000::/1) through the tunnel, so
    other clients' default routes no longer take the traffic.
  * Store the subscription of a profile in vpn.data: netplan lost the user
    setting, so updates created every server again. Remove the duplicates.

 -- Sevan A. <42666637+s11va9@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0700

network-manager-vless (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add an authentication helper: GNOME Settings no longer waits 25 seconds
    when opening a VLESS connection.
  * Restart Xray-core automatically if it exits while connected.
  * Keep DNS queries inside the tunnel (negative DNS priority).
  * Send the server the domain of each connection (sniffing), as other Xray
    clients do; sites routed by domain on the server failed before.
  * Warn about proxy environment variables that point to a local proxy.
  * Log the service and xray to the journal (NetworkManager drops their output).
  * Add "nm-vless test" to check sites through a server without connecting.
  * Move DNS of existing subscription profiles into the tunnel on update.

 -- Sevan A. <42666637+s11va9@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 17:00:00 +0300

network-manager-vless (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add subscriptions (https:// URLs) from the GNOME Settings editor.
  * Update each subscription at the interval requested by the provider.
  * Warn about other tunnels and system proxies that bypass the VPN.

